WEBVTT

1
00:59:46.370 --> 00:59:47.370
Hallelujah.

2
00:59:47.370 --> 00:59:55.890
I may introduce the collection today.

3
00:59:55.890 --> 01:00:03.610
And I wanted to bring a piece, to explore a bit about faith.

4
01:00:03.610 --> 01:00:09.650
Just as Pastor Tim just mentioned, believing is often a struggle between two extremes.

5
01:00:09.650 --> 01:00:13.570
Faith can clash hard against common sense.

6
01:00:13.570 --> 01:00:19.130
And even in that, you can lose your way and start to drift.

7
01:00:19.130 --> 01:00:26.610
But you also have common sense that can clash hard against faith, that is rationalism,

8
01:00:26.610 --> 01:00:28.850
where faith simply has no room at all.

9
01:00:28.850 --> 01:00:35.850
And both extremes are never intended in that way by the Father.

10
01:00:35.850 --> 01:00:42.250
For it is just like with love, faith is just like with love, it is also based

11
01:00:42.250 --> 01:00:43.250
on love.

12
01:00:43.930 --> 01:00:45.930
And do you know what it is?

13
01:00:45.930 --> 01:00:52.250
Just like love, it is intended that we love the Father with all our heart,

14
01:00:52.250 --> 01:00:54.050
with all our soul, and with all our mind.

15
01:00:54.050 --> 01:00:56.850
And it is the same with faith.

16
01:00:56.850 --> 01:01:02.370
We should not do that in boxes and categories, but we should do that with all our heart,

17
01:01:02.370 --> 01:01:04.010
with all our soul, and with all our mind.

18
01:01:04.010 --> 01:01:10.810
Know that Paul places three phenomena side by side that will last forever.

19
01:01:10.810 --> 01:01:12.770
That is faith, hope, and love.

20
01:01:13.770 --> 01:01:17.170
And love and faith, they are connected to each other.

21
01:01:17.170 --> 01:01:19.490
Do you know what it is?

22
01:01:19.490 --> 01:01:23.930
If we do this with all our heart, with all our soul, and with all our mind, then it speaks

23
01:01:23.930 --> 01:01:25.170
of surrender as well.

24
01:01:25.170 --> 01:01:31.450
For we must not think that we can love the Father with all our heart, with all our mind, and

25
01:01:31.450 --> 01:01:34.810
with all our soul, because we are unworthy.

26
01:01:34.810 --> 01:01:37.290
We cannot manage that as humans.

27
01:01:37.290 --> 01:01:39.610
So we need Jesus.

28
01:01:39.610 --> 01:01:42.250
We always need Jesus.

29
01:01:42.730 --> 01:01:43.690
In every situation.

30
01:01:43.690 --> 01:01:52.570
And it is also true that the texts I have today are about faith.

31
01:01:52.570 --> 01:01:57.570
And the beautiful thing is, in those three, common sense is not included.

32
01:01:57.570 --> 01:01:58.690
There is faith, hope, and love.

33
01:01:58.690 --> 01:02:00.730
There is no common sense included, or understanding.

34
01:02:00.730 --> 01:02:04.570
Love goes beyond understanding as well.

35
01:02:04.570 --> 01:02:11.370
Otherwise, very few people might step into the boat together.

36
01:02:11.490 --> 01:02:13.650
No, but it goes further.

37
01:02:13.650 --> 01:02:16.450
It is not a mathematical thing, not a science.

38
01:02:16.450 --> 01:02:17.810
It goes further.

39
01:02:17.810 --> 01:02:20.650
It goes to your heart, it goes to your soul, and to your mind.

40
01:02:20.650 --> 01:02:22.970
And God intended those three to be together.

41
01:02:22.970 --> 01:02:25.210
So He made us.

42
01:02:25.210 --> 01:02:27.130
That is His recipe, that is His concept.

43
01:02:27.130 --> 01:02:32.890
And I find it very beautiful to be able to present this this morning, as we look at

44
01:02:32.890 --> 01:02:33.410
the texts.

45
01:02:33.410 --> 01:02:37.970
I have asked for Hebrews 11 verse 1 and also verse 6.

46
01:02:37.970 --> 01:02:43.970
I don't know if they could be projected, but it is very beautiful.

47
01:02:43.970 --> 01:02:47.490
In verse 1 is the definition of faith.

48
01:02:47.490 --> 01:02:53.370
Faith, just as Pastor Tim just indicated, is the certainty that the things we expect,

49
01:02:53.370 --> 01:02:56.530
or hope for, will also become reality.

50
01:02:56.530 --> 01:03:00.810
It is the evidence of things we do not yet see.

51
01:03:00.810 --> 01:03:06.010
And this makes faith mindblowing.

52
01:03:06.050 --> 01:03:11.850
And then it says a little further on, because there are many examples of how faith

53
01:03:11.850 --> 01:03:14.930
has manifested in great men and women of God.

54
01:03:14.930 --> 01:03:19.690
And then you have one, who is still there, who found God so delightful that He took him away.

55
01:03:19.690 --> 01:03:25.450
And it says there why he made God happy.

56
01:03:25.450 --> 01:03:29.010
If we believe with all our heart, all our soul, and all our mind, then we make God

57
01:03:29.010 --> 01:03:30.010
happy.

58
01:03:30.010 --> 01:03:31.850
For we trust Him.

59
01:03:31.850 --> 01:03:38.290
And as we look, it says there, but if someone does not have faith, God cannot possibly

60
01:03:38.290 --> 01:03:39.290
be happy with him.

61
01:03:39.290 --> 01:03:43.570
If we do not trust him, it hurts.

62
01:03:43.570 --> 01:03:46.690
It is logical that he cannot be there, that he can be happy with that.

63
01:03:46.690 --> 01:03:53.170
For when someone comes to God, he must believe that he is who he says he is.

64
01:03:53.170 --> 01:03:56.370
And that he rewards those who truly long for him.

65
01:03:56.370 --> 01:03:58.930
This is such a beautiful text.

66
01:03:59.730 --> 01:04:02.570
It also speaks of surrender, that longing.

67
01:04:02.570 --> 01:04:09.930
And why is it relatively easy to believe, when you have truly come to know that dear father, that

68
01:04:09.930 --> 01:04:11.930
good good father.

69
01:04:11.930 --> 01:04:18.450
That is because Jesus has given us the right image of the Father and still gives it.

70
01:04:18.450 --> 01:04:20.810
As the Father truly is.

71
01:04:20.810 --> 01:04:22.530
And that he stands behind us.

72
01:04:22.530 --> 01:04:28.450
Because then we have the assurance that he is a fulfiller of his word.

73
01:04:29.450 --> 01:04:32.090
And his word is truth.

74
01:04:32.090 --> 01:04:36.050
And we may fully believe in that and trust wholeheartedly.

75
01:04:36.050 --> 01:04:41.050
And that is for his children the evidence of things we cannot see with the naked eye.

76
01:04:41.050 --> 01:04:42.050
And the assurance of things we hope for or expect.

77
01:04:42.050 --> 01:04:45.210
And that applies to all subjects in the Bible, it applies to our salvation, applies to forgiveness,

78
01:04:45.210 --> 01:04:53.330
applies to healing, atonement, but also in bringing back.

79
01:04:53.330 --> 01:04:56.490
We may also do that with our whole heart in that faith.

80
01:04:56.530 --> 01:05:00.410


81
01:05:00.410 --> 01:05:02.330
For faith is a total package.

82
01:05:02.330 --> 01:05:05.770
And we ourselves are also a total package for the Father.

83
01:05:05.770 --> 01:05:07.170
Everything in life belongs to that.

84
01:05:07.170 --> 01:05:13.450
And when we bring it back in faith, we show that if we believe in Him and His Word and His

85
01:05:13.450 --> 01:05:18.370
instructions and also act on them, you trust the Father.

86
01:05:18.370 --> 01:05:19.690
And that makes Him happy.

87
01:05:19.690 --> 01:05:24.730
And then He also makes His Word true for you.

88
01:05:24.730 --> 01:05:25.730
In His way.

89
01:05:26.730 --> 01:05:28.730
And I want to bless us with that.

90
01:05:28.730 --> 01:05:29.730
Also in bringing it back.

91
01:05:29.730 --> 01:05:34.730
Maybe it is also nice to stand for a moment and to thank in reverence for that.

92
01:05:36.730 --> 01:05:41.730
Thank you, Father, for sending your own Son.

93
01:05:42.730 --> 01:05:44.730
You allowed Him to be crushed.

94
01:05:44.730 --> 01:05:46.730
He looked unrecognizable.

95
01:05:48.730 --> 01:05:49.730
Why?

96
01:05:49.730 --> 01:05:52.730
So that we would become recognizable again to the Father.

97
01:05:56.730 --> 01:06:00.730
We are your children.

98
01:06:00.730 --> 01:06:04.730
And you see Jesus in us.

99
01:06:04.730 --> 01:06:07.730
And that makes you happy.

100
01:06:07.730 --> 01:06:11.730
Not that we will never rely on our own understanding.

101
01:06:11.730 --> 01:06:14.730
But that we will build on Jesus.

102
01:06:14.730 --> 01:06:15.730
And Jesus alone.

103
01:06:15.730 --> 01:06:20.730
And I pray that we may also do that with what we can bring back from earthly things.

104
01:06:20.730 --> 01:06:23.730
That we may build on Jesus with that.

105
01:06:23.730 --> 01:06:25.730
Actually madness, but it is so beautiful.

106
01:06:25.730 --> 01:06:27.730
And so you intended it.

107
01:06:27.730 --> 01:06:28.730
Very why?

108
01:06:28.730 --> 01:06:29.730
Because you want our whole heart.

109
01:06:29.730 --> 01:06:30.730
Our whole soul.

110
01:06:30.730 --> 01:06:31.730
And our whole mind.

111
01:06:31.730 --> 01:06:33.730
And I bless us with that in Jesus' name.

112
01:06:48.730 --> 01:06:49.730
Glory to God.

113
01:06:50.730 --> 01:06:51.730
Glory to God.

114
01:06:53.730 --> 01:06:54.730
Do you have your Bible with you?

115
01:06:55.730 --> 01:07:00.730
Then we will finish our Bible study of the letter to the Ephesians together.

116
01:07:03.730 --> 01:07:09.730
All the people who were baptized last week, would you please stand up.

117
01:07:10.730 --> 01:07:13.730
The baptized from last week, would you please stand up.

118
01:07:15.730 --> 01:07:16.730
Good, good, good.

119
01:07:18.730 --> 01:07:19.730
Warlord.

120
01:07:24.730 --> 01:07:26.730
I want to pray for you.

121
01:07:26.730 --> 01:07:27.730
I want to pray for you.

122
01:07:28.730 --> 01:07:29.730
Please remain standing for a moment.

123
01:07:30.730 --> 01:07:35.730
Lord, I want to pray for our new brothers and sisters.

124
01:07:35.730 --> 01:07:39.730
Lord, that they will be blessed with the blood of Christ.

125
01:07:39.730 --> 01:07:43.730
Over their soul, over their body, and over their spirit.

126
01:07:43.730 --> 01:07:46.730
Lord, that the enemy may not rob them.

127
01:07:46.730 --> 01:07:48.730
Lord, and that they will not be.

128
01:07:49.730 --> 01:07:52.730
I declare over you that you will not be.

129
01:07:52.730 --> 01:07:56.730
Like the seed that falls on the path, or the rocks, or the thorns.

130
01:07:57.730 --> 01:08:00.730
Satan will not be able to steal you, in the name of Jesus.

131
01:08:01.730 --> 01:08:04.730
But you will be grounded in good soil.

132
01:08:05.730 --> 01:08:09.730
I prophesy and proclaim over your life that your roots will go deep.

133
01:08:10.730 --> 01:08:14.730
That you will never look away, except to the cross.

134
01:08:14.730 --> 01:08:18.730
Nothing more than the blood of Jesus.

135
01:08:45.730 --> 01:08:49.730
I also tell you that your eyes will be opened wide,

136
01:08:49.730 --> 01:08:54.730
that your spiritual eyes will understand the Scripture, will fathom it.

137
01:08:54.730 --> 01:08:57.730
That it will not be flat text for you,

138
01:08:57.730 --> 01:09:01.730
but that you will experience the depth of God's Word in your lives.

139
01:09:02.730 --> 01:09:05.730
That you will experience revelation upon revelation.

140
01:09:06.730 --> 01:09:10.730
But above all, and this is what almost the entire New Testament is about,

141
01:09:10.730 --> 01:09:13.730
above all, that you will persevere.

142
01:09:13.730 --> 01:09:17.730
Perseverance. Perseverance in the name of Jesus.

143
01:09:18.730 --> 01:09:20.730
No more going back to the world.

144
01:09:20.730 --> 01:09:23.730
I claim no more going back to the world.

145
01:09:23.730 --> 01:09:25.730
In the name of Jesus.

146
01:09:25.730 --> 01:09:28.730
And lastly, I want to encourage you alongside this prayer, amen,

147
01:09:28.730 --> 01:09:30.730
but lastly, I want to encourage you.

148
01:09:31.730 --> 01:09:35.730
Should you ever find yourselves in valleys and stay away,

149
01:09:35.730 --> 01:09:37.730
the church comes after you.

150
01:09:37.730 --> 01:09:40.730
And you may call this stalking, but we come after you.

151
01:09:40.730 --> 01:09:42.730
And I mean that seriously.

152
01:09:42.730 --> 01:09:46.730
Also allow the church to sharpen you.

153
01:09:46.730 --> 01:09:49.730
That when things are wrong, you will be sharpened.

154
01:09:49.730 --> 01:09:52.730
The Bible says, iron sharpens iron.

155
01:09:52.730 --> 01:09:55.730
That your soul will also be prepared,

156
01:09:55.730 --> 01:09:59.730
that when God's Word needs to set something right in your life,

157
01:09:59.730 --> 01:10:02.730
or when the church comes to set something right in your life,

158
01:10:02.730 --> 01:10:04.730
that you will not harden yourself,

159
01:10:04.730 --> 01:10:07.730
but that you will be moldable, that you will have a soft heart.

160
01:10:07.730 --> 01:10:10.730
For the King of Kings, in Jesus' name.

161
01:10:10.730 --> 01:10:12.730
Amen? Amen.

162
01:10:12.730 --> 01:10:14.730
Praise the name of Jesus.

163
01:10:16.730 --> 01:10:18.730
All right, if you have your Bible with you,

164
01:10:18.730 --> 01:10:22.730
please turn with me to Ephesians, chapter 6.

165
01:10:22.730 --> 01:10:27.730
We are going to conclude the letter of Paul to the Ephesians.

166
01:10:29.730 --> 01:10:31.730
With the last chapter.

167
01:10:32.730 --> 01:10:34.730
With the last chapter.

168
01:10:34.730 --> 01:10:37.730
And God has timed this well.

169
01:10:38.730 --> 01:10:44.730
Because last weekend was totally Halloween.

170
01:10:45.730 --> 01:10:48.730
But there was just nothing to it.

171
01:10:49.730 --> 01:10:51.730
And I find that funny.

172
01:10:52.730 --> 01:10:55.730
And I believe in the power of prayer.

173
01:10:55.730 --> 01:10:57.730
And I just believe in it.

174
01:10:57.730 --> 01:11:00.730
And I have seen it in my neighborhood.

175
01:11:00.730 --> 01:11:04.730
That in the past years there were ghost tours held.

176
01:11:04.730 --> 01:11:09.730
And even in the field next to my house, at one point in previous years,

177
01:11:09.730 --> 01:11:11.730
there was a kind of fire set up.

178
01:11:11.730 --> 01:11:13.730
With LED lights and ugly, whatever.

179
01:11:13.730 --> 01:11:17.730
And then, it was a thing in our neighborhood.

180
01:11:17.730 --> 01:11:20.730


181
01:11:20.730 --> 01:11:24.730
And I have no need for that.

182
01:11:24.730 --> 01:11:27.730
For it is a feast of death.

183
01:11:27.730 --> 01:11:29.730
It is a feast of fear.

184
01:11:29.730 --> 01:11:30.730
There is...

185
01:11:30.730 --> 01:11:34.730
Why, if we want to steal parties from America,

186
01:11:34.730 --> 01:11:37.730
why don't we steal Thanksgiving?

187
01:11:37.730 --> 01:11:39.730
It's a much better feast, isn't it?

188
01:11:39.730 --> 01:11:42.730
At least they have good food.

189
01:11:42.730 --> 01:11:43.730
You know what I mean?

190
01:11:43.730 --> 01:11:45.730
That's just nonsense, right?

191
01:11:45.730 --> 01:11:52.730
And who wants to decorate their house with skulls and spider webs?

192
01:11:52.730 --> 01:11:55.730
There is something sick about it.

193
01:11:55.730 --> 01:11:57.730
And when people say, it's just trick or treat.

194
01:11:57.730 --> 01:12:00.730
Listen, if you want candy, just knock, you'll get candy.

195
01:12:00.730 --> 01:12:02.730
And then I'll close the door again.

196
01:12:02.730 --> 01:12:04.730
But it's just sick.

197
01:12:04.730 --> 01:12:08.730
And I will... Here is one thing, huh.

198
01:12:08.730 --> 01:12:11.730
I was walking in the Delhaize in Pelt.

199
01:12:11.730 --> 01:12:16.730
And normally in Pelt, at the Delhaize, they decorate the corner very extensively.

200
01:12:16.730 --> 01:12:20.730
Very extensively, super scary.

201
01:12:20.730 --> 01:12:24.730
And this time it wasn't like that.

202
01:12:24.730 --> 01:12:26.730
In the end, they did hang something up.

203
01:12:26.730 --> 01:12:30.730
I think in the rush or something they did throw something in the corner after all.

204
01:12:30.730 --> 01:12:34.730
But in all of October it wasn't there yet, at the beginning.

205
01:12:34.730 --> 01:12:36.730
And here is the thing.

206
01:12:36.730 --> 01:12:38.730
The world is loud.

207
01:12:38.730 --> 01:12:40.730
The world just keeps chattering.

208
01:12:40.730 --> 01:12:42.730
It all borrows things from each other.

209
01:12:42.730 --> 01:12:44.730
And it all stirs each other up.

210
01:12:44.730 --> 01:12:47.730
But if Christians just don't open their mouths,

211
01:12:47.730 --> 01:12:51.730
then you don't let your voice be heard in this world.

212
01:12:51.730 --> 01:12:54.730
So we need to be vocal.

213
01:12:54.730 --> 01:12:56.730
We need to open our mouths.

214
01:12:56.730 --> 01:12:58.730
You have to make your opinion known.

215
01:12:58.730 --> 01:13:01.730
I know we live in a shouting society,

216
01:13:01.730 --> 01:13:04.730
where everyone has an opinion and everyone talks.

217
01:13:04.730 --> 01:13:08.730
But let Christians please be loud about the light of Christ.

218
01:13:08.730 --> 01:13:11.730
So I walked into the Delhaize and I said...

219
01:13:11.730 --> 01:13:15.730
Hey, that corner of yours, hasn't it been decorated with...

220
01:13:15.730 --> 01:13:17.730
With... Buh.

221
01:13:17.730 --> 01:13:19.730
No, I didn't say it like that.

222
01:13:19.730 --> 01:13:22.730
I just said, isn't that corner of yours decorated for Halloween?

223
01:13:22.730 --> 01:13:25.730
And then someone said, no, no, yeah, busy and so on.

224
01:13:25.730 --> 01:13:27.730
And then I said, no, don't do that.

225
01:13:27.730 --> 01:13:29.730
I said, you especially shouldn't do it for me.

226
01:13:29.730 --> 01:13:31.730
Because it's a bad holiday.

227
01:13:31.730 --> 01:13:33.730
And it's a holiday of fear.

228
01:13:33.730 --> 01:13:36.730
It's a holiday celebrating death.

229
01:13:36.730 --> 01:13:39.730
And I also just say in the world, even though they don't understand that word,

230
01:13:39.730 --> 01:13:41.730
it's an occult holiday.

231
01:13:41.730 --> 01:13:45.730
And it leaves traces and it really scares children.

232
01:13:45.730 --> 01:13:47.730
And this is also proven in psychology.

233
01:13:47.730 --> 01:13:49.730
Children really become afraid of it.

234
01:13:49.730 --> 01:13:51.730
Depression increases.

235
01:13:51.730 --> 01:13:53.730
And occultism increases.

236
01:13:53.730 --> 01:13:57.730
And people with a background in occultism,

237
01:13:57.730 --> 01:14:00.730
people who have been in Wicca and in witchcraft,

238
01:14:00.730 --> 01:14:03.730
testify how foolish Christians can sometimes be,

239
01:14:03.730 --> 01:14:05.730
especially in North America.

240
01:14:05.730 --> 01:14:08.730
Because the Wiccans of old who have come to repentance,

241
01:14:08.730 --> 01:14:10.730
testify just so often,

242
01:14:10.730 --> 01:14:14.730
by saying that Halloween is a time of demonism.

243
01:14:14.730 --> 01:14:16.730
So it's not, oh, it's just trick or treat.

244
01:14:16.730 --> 01:14:19.730
That is exactly what Satan does every time.

245
01:14:19.730 --> 01:14:22.730
Disguising something, making it seem fun,

246
01:14:22.730 --> 01:14:24.730
a little candy on the side,

247
01:14:24.730 --> 01:14:26.730
he presents himself as an angel of light,

248
01:14:26.730 --> 01:14:29.730
but in the meantime, he brings you death.

249
01:14:29.730 --> 01:14:31.730
This is exactly what he does.

250
01:14:31.730 --> 01:14:33.730
And then at one point I say to that woman,

251
01:14:33.730 --> 01:14:35.730
don't do it, because it's a useless celebration,

252
01:14:35.730 --> 01:14:37.730
children get scared of it,

253
01:14:37.730 --> 01:14:39.730
so for me, you shouldn't do this,

254
01:14:39.730 --> 01:14:41.730
